den","title":"Saturday: Spot the Living-History Garden","subtitle":"1812 Garden · Hamilton College Community Farm","notes":"Find the split-rail enclosure and observe the garden from established paths; leave plants, tools, and active growing areas undisturbed.","short_summary":"See how a small cultivated space supports hands-on historical study.","evidence_claim":"Hamilton’s Community Farm identifies the 1812 Garden as a 40-by-60-foot, split-rail-enclosed section in the garden’s northwest corner.","source_url":"https://students.hamilton.edu/communityfarm/almanac/farm-work/farm-layout","source_title":"Hamilton College Community Farm — Farm Layout","source_kind":"student_media","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Treat the farm as an active educational growing site; remain on established access routes and follow posted instructions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"clinton-kirkland-town-library","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Kirkland Town Library","title":"Saturday: Connect with Clinton’s Library","subtitle":"Kirkland Town Library · 55½ College Street","notes":"Visit during posted Saturday hours, browse the community collection, and note which resources require a Mid York library account to borrow.","short_summary":"Meet the wider Clinton community through its public library.","evidence_claim":"Kirkland Town Library lists its address as 55½ College Street in Clinton and describes collections, technology, games, and community resources.","source_url":"https://www.kirklandtownlibrary.org/home","source_title":"Kirkland Town Library","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The library currently posts Saturday hours of 10 a.m.–2 p.m.; verify special closings before leaving campus. Borrowing may require registration.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hamilton-root-glen","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Root Glen","title":"Sunday: Close with a Root Glen Walk","subtitle":"Root Glen · shale paths and campus arboretum","notes":"Take a daylight walk on the shale path, notice changes in tree and shrub species, and turn back if weather makes the surface difficult.","short_summary":"End the weekend with a landscape-focused campus loop.","evidence_claim":"Hamilton describes Root Glen as a forested campus area with a shale walkway, roughly 65 tree species, dozens of shrubs, and many flower varieties.","source_url":"https://www.hamilton.edu/about/sustainability/root-glen-and-arboretum","source_title":"Root Glen and Arboretum","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use established paths in daylight and adjust for rain, snow, ice, maintenance activity, or posted closures.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
